title: 'statement-store: serve peers without the v2 DHT path in a mixed network'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    With the v2 DHT path on, a full statement/2 peer that sends no filter within the grace period
    is treated as a node without the DHT path: it gets every statement, a match-all filter in
    return so it floods everything back, and it leaves the DHT index. A late filter restores it.
    A statement/1 peer is served the same way from the start and gets no filter. The gauge
    `substrate_sync_statement_peers_without_dht` counts such peers.
crates:
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: patch
